# B9 for demo.ifms.dev (Cloudflare Tunnel, no CloudFront on the API path). Path of a request:
#   browser -> Cloudflare edge (sets CF-Connecting-IP) -> cloudflared (IFMS stack) -> sangam-front (nginx, keeps the
#   header, adds X-Forwarded-For) -> sangam-server (peer = sangam-front on sangam-internal).
# The server reads CF-Connecting-IP / X-Forwarded-For only from a peer listed here (TrustedProxyFilter, SL-18), so:
#   1. the sangam-internal subnet (the front, the only peer that reaches the server; SANGAM_INTERNAL_SUBNET);
#   2. the Cloudflare published ranges, so a walk of X-Forwarded-For stops at the edge.
# VERIFY the Cloudflare lists at deploy time against https://www.cloudflare.com/ips-v4 and /ips-v6 (they were
# copied from Cloudflare's published list; a change there must be copied here). No CloudFront ranges.
# sangam-front is never published on a host port, so nothing but cloudflared can set these headers.
SANGAM_CLIENT_IP_HEADERS=CF-Connecting-IP,X-Forwarded-For
SANGAM_TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.29.250.0/24,173.245.48.0/20,103.21.244.0/22,103.22.200.0/22,103.31.4.0/22,141.101.64.0/18,108.162.192.0/18,190.93.240.0/20,188.114.96.0/20,197.234.240.0/22,198.41.128.0/17,162.158.0.0/15,104.16.0.0/13,104.24.0.0/14,172.64.0.0/13,131.0.72.0/22,2400:cb00::/32,2606:4700::/32,2803:f800::/32,2405:b500::/32,2405:8100::/32,2a06:98c0::/29,2c0f:f248::/32
